# A descending three-clause loop must count down: `i > stop` with a decreasing
# post clause, and it must run zero times when start == stop.
#
# HISTORY: this was `range()`-with-a-negative-step until 2026-07-29. The original
# regression it caught was tychoc0 hardcoding `i < stop`, so range(3, 0, -1) never
# ran. Phase 6 of the loops-cleanup plan rewrote the three
# descending sites to `for i := a; i > b; i -= s:` — the same iteration sequences
# and the SAME golden, which is what makes the rewrite checkable. Note the direction
# is now spelled by the author in the condition rather than inferred from the sign
# of a step, so the class of bug this file was written for cannot recur here;
# what it guards now is that the author-written descending form works.
fn main():
    for i := 3; i > 0; i -= 1:
        print(str(i))
    for i := 10; i > 0; i -= 3:
        print(str(i))
    for i := 0; i < 3; i += 1:
        print(str(i))
    n := 0
    for i := 5; i > 5; i -= 1:
        n = n + 1
    print("empty " + str(n))
